---
source: tests/golden.rs
---
  x the pin says nothing about how it is kept current
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:13:13]
 12 |         module "loose" {
 13 |             pin {
    :             ^|^
    :              `-- needs `renovate` or `manual`
 14 |                 url "http://example.com/modules.zip"
    `----
  help: `renovate datasource="github-tags" depName="owner/repo"`, or `manual
        "why nothing tracks it"`

  x the pin declares no `version`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:13:13]
 12 |         module "loose" {
 13 |             pin {
    :             ^|^
    :              `-- nothing pinned
 14 |                 url "http://example.com/modules.zip"
    `----
  help: an exact tag or commit; a moving ref would make the build depend on
        when it ran

  x the pin declares no `sha256`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:13:13]
 12 |         module "loose" {
 13 |             pin {
    :             ^|^
    :              `-- nothing to verify what arrived
 14 |                 url "http://example.com/modules.zip"
    `----
  help: a remote module is arbitrary shell running as root in the build, so
        the content hash is required, not optional

  x the URL is not https
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:13:13]
 12 |         module "loose" {
 13 |             pin {
    :             ^|^
    :              `-- unencrypted or unsupported scheme
 14 |                 url "http://example.com/modules.zip"
    `----
  help: https://, or file:// for a local archive

  x the pin is not a tar archive
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:13:13]
 12 |         module "loose" {
 13 |             pin {
    :             ^|^
    :              `-- cannot be extracted
 14 |                 url "http://example.com/modules.zip"
    `----
  help: one of .tar.gz, .tgz, .tar.xz, .tar.zst, .tar.bz2; the fetch strips
        the archive's leading directory, which is a tar option

  x invalid subtree path `/etc/passwd`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:13:13]
 12 |         module "loose" {
 13 |             pin {
    :             ^|^
    :              `-- relative to the archive root, so it cannot start with /
 14 |                 url "http://example.com/modules.zip"
    `----
  help: `path "modules/module-name"`, the module's directory inside the
        repository

  x `loose` is not fetched
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-pin/image.kdl:12:9]
 11 |     modules {
 12 |         module "loose" {
    :         ^^^|^^
    :            `-- no module.kdl here yet
 13 |             pin {
    `----
  help: run ./generated/scripts/tect.sh fetch modules to fetch what the image
        references
